{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"system","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","text":"MXLSystemRelation","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"system","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"particular part where the element appears."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/system","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/system"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"system","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"system","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV6systemAA17MXLSystemRelationOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/system":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"system","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/system","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"particular part where the element appears.","type":"text"}],"title":"system","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/system"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemRelation":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation type distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the particular","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part where the element appears. A value of only-top indicates that the element should appear only on the top","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part of the current system. A value of also-top indicates that the element should appear on both the current","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part and the top part of the current system. If this value appears in a score, when parts are created the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element should only appear once in this part, not twice. A value of none indicates that the element is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated only with the current part, not with the system.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemRelation"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemRelation"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation","title":"MXLSystemRelation","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemrelation"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLEnding","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending"}}}